1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,760
If you put a motor

2
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:02,140
inside a dead bird,

3
00:00:02,180 --> 00:00:02,680
you could make it

4
00:00:02,720 --> 00:00:04,070
fly again.

5
00:00:04,110 --> 00:00:05,265
Researchers built drones

6
00:00:05,305 --> 00:00:06,950
using preserved bird bodies,

7
00:00:06,990 --> 00:00:07,895
with machinery hidden

8
00:00:07,935 --> 00:00:09,320
underneath the feathers.

9
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:10,175
A gearbox turns

10
00:00:10,215 --> 00:00:11,375
the motor’s spinning motion

11
00:00:11,415 --> 00:00:12,910
into flapping wings.

12
00:00:12,950 --> 00:00:13,420
The goal is

13
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:14,380
to watch wildlife

14
00:00:14,420 --> 00:00:15,900
with less disturbance.

15
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:16,575
And they’ve built

16
00:00:16,615 --> 00:00:17,455
a swimming robot

17
00:00:17,495 --> 00:00:19,090
using a preserved duck.

18
00:00:19,130 --> 00:00:19,905
So the bird

19
00:00:19,945 --> 00:00:21,410
watching the birds…

20
00:00:21,450 --> 00:00:22,900
might already be dead.

